# E336 - Transparent accounting for target-ABI conditional upstream skips

id:                     E413
trigger_tool:           test|runtime
phase:                  testing
error_signature:        ok .* # SKIP|expected skip.*counted as PASS|tests must be fully executed and pass N/N

severity:               2
category:               limitation, portability, testing
match_keywords:         expected SKIP, conditional skip, upstream inventory, nonfailed, AArch64, UINT_MAX, SIZE_MAX, GLib TAP
title:                  Keep target-ABI conditional upstream skips visible in the full inventory

root_cause:             A fixed upstream inventory can contain cases that are
                        intentionally inapplicable on a target ABI. Treating a
                        TAP skip as PASS inflates coverage, while shrinking the
                        denominator hides registered tests. Registered, passed,
                        skipped, failed, and nonfailed counts are distinct facts.
affected_scope:         Cross-platform upstream suites whose registered cases
                        conditionally skip when the target ABI or public API
                        cannot express the requested operation.
verification_cmd:       Freeze the complete inventory plus exact expected-skip
                        IDs, paths, and reasons; require passed + skipped = total,
                        failed = 0, and report every outcome separately.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           hashed-expected-skip-outcome-contract
rec_description:        Preserve the full registered denominator, accept a skip
                        only when its stable ID, path, and diagnostic match the
                        hashed allowlist, reject unexpected skips or passes, and
                        publish passed, skipped, failed, total, and nonfailed.
rec_command:            Validate TAP or JUnit output against a hashed inventory and expected-skip allowlist.
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               test-result-validator

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      upstream-capability-split
fallback_description:   If upstream supports capability-specific test groups,
                        run and report each official group separately while
                        retaining the complete registered inventory.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       skip.*PASS|passed_count.*nonfailed|N/N.*100%.*SKIP
forbid_1_reason:        A skipped case did not execute its asserted behavior and
                        cannot truthfully be counted as passed.
forbid_1_consequence:   The reported pass rate and coverage evidence are inflated.
forbid_2_pattern:       inventory.*minus.*skip|total.*runnable|16/16.*upstream
forbid_2_reason:        Removing conditional skips from the denominator hides
                        stable upstream registrations and masks ABI limitations.
forbid_2_consequence:   Reviewers cannot reconcile the report with upstream.

principles:             P010,P013

causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             [E228]
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []

